# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
#
# SECURITY (P4):
#   * .env is ignored by .gitignore - NEVER commit real credentials.
#   * Only the local .env may contain a real key. Never paste a key into
#     config.yaml, source code, tests, README, chat, or an issue.
#   * Before committing, run: python -m src.utils.secret_guard
#   * If a key ever leaks, revoke it at https://openrouter.ai/keys at once.
#
# Scope of .env: secrets and service endpoints ONLY.
# Everything else lives in config.yaml (model, paths, retrieval, seed) - except
# the adaptive policy's own constants, which live in src/agent/policy.py so the
# method has exactly one definition.
#
# The platform connects to the LLM BY DEFAULT: once this key is filled in,
# `python -m src.agent.run` uses OpenRouter with no extra flag. If the key is
# missing/placeholder the run prints these steps and exits 2 (no silent
# downgrade); `python -m src.agent.run --offline` is the only no-key escape.
#
# The product path uses a PAID OpenRouter model: deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash
# (config.yaml -> llm.model), with z-ai/glm-5.3-flash as the cross-vendor
# fallback. Approx. $0.0002 per decision. Free IDs were dropped after they
# turned out to be the main source of 429s and truncated replies. To browse
# zero-cost alternatives anyway:
#   python -m src.utils.llm_client --list-free-models
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works: point OPENROUTER_BASE_URL at the
# local/other service and put its key in OPENROUTER_API_KEY.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your-key-here
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
